@startuml
' Figure 5.4 – System sequence diagram: AI conversation grounded in the writer's own corpus
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram AI chat with retrieval
autonumber "0 :"

participant "Writer" as R
participant "System" as A
participant "Embedding\nprovider" as E
participant "Language\nmodel" as L
participant "Database" as D

ref over R, D : Sign in

R -> A : Type a question in the AI panel
activate A
A -> A : Check and grant the daily AI allowance
A -> E : Embed the question (1536 dimensions)
activate E
E --> A : Query vector
deactivate E
A -> D : Retrieve the writer's own passages\n(cosine distance, top-K = 5, similarity >= 0.60)
D --> A : 5 passages, top similarity 0.668
A -> D : Read the writer's voice profile
D --> A : Tone, style, vocabulary, topics

alt allowance exhausted
  A --> R : Display the quota notice and disable the composer
else allowance available
  A -> A : Assemble the prompt\nROLE + MEMORY + PASSAGES + QUESTION (~2000 tokens)
  A -> L : Stream a completion
activate L
  loop for each generated chunk
    L --> A : Chunk
    A --> R : Server-sent event, rendered incrementally
  end
  L --> A : End of stream and tokens consumed
deactivate L
  A -> D : Record the interaction and decrement the balance
  A --> R : Passages used, grouped by article
  deactivate A
end

note over R, D
  No training takes place: articles are embedded and retrieved
  at query time, so an article published a minute ago is
  immediately usable.
end note
@enduml
